That file holds pairwise frequencies derived from allele frequencies and D. The phased frequencies in the next
section supersede it.

## Phased haplotype frequencies

These come directly from phased 1000 Genomes phase 3 European genotypes (503 samples, 1,006 chromosomes,
via the Ensembl REST API), then are rescaled to the gnomAD v4 non-Finnish-European allele frequencies that the
project uses as primary. Rescaling is by iterative proportional fitting, which keeps the odds-ratio structure
of the observed table, moves only the allele frequencies, and works for three loci. A haplotype that is
absent in 1000G stays absent.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
hp <- read.csv("data/haplotype_frequencies_phased.csv")
ldp <- read.csv("data/haplotype_ld_phased.csv")
```
:::


### PTX3, three loci

Alleles are in the order rs2305619, rs3816527, rs1840680.


::: {#tbl-trio .cell tbl-cap='PTX3 three-locus haplotypes. SE is the binomial standard error on 1,006 chromosomes.'}

```{.r .cell-code}
hp |>
  filter(block == "PTX3_trio", n_chromosomes > 0) |>
  arrange(desc(freq_1000G_EUR)) |>
  transmute(Haplotype = haplotype, Chromosomes = n_chromosomes,
            `1000G EUR` = freq_1000G_EUR, SE = se_1000G_EUR, `gnomAD NFE (rescaled)` = freq_gnomAD_NFE_rescaled) |>
  gt() |>
  fmt_number(c(`1000G EUR`, SE, `gnomAD NFE (rescaled)`), decimals = 4)
```

