There are three common haplotypes, not two. rs2305619 A and rs1840680 A mark the same class of chromosome
(r² = 0.996), which is A-C-A plus A-A-A. rs3816527 C splits that class, and A-C-A is about 87% of it. The
single A-A-G chromosome is too rare to estimate; its rescaled frequency is fixed by the margins alone.

